## 1. ROOT CAUSE AUDIT EVIDENCE

### Issue A: "Antigravity Hub response timed out after 45s."
In `app/src/main/java/com/jarvisai/assistant/data/remote/AntigravityApiService.kt` (lines 293–382):
```kotlin
var pollAttempts = 0
val maxAttempts = 45 // 45 seconds timeout
val pollPayload = JSONObject().put("cascadeId", cascadeId).toString()

while (!turnFinished && pollAttempts < maxAttempts) {
    delay(1000)
    pollAttempts++
    ...
}
if (!turnFinished) {
    emit(AntigravityStreamEvent.Error("Antigravity Hub response timed out after ${maxAttempts}s."))
}
```
**Why this breaks on big tasks:**
- A complex instruction or long prompt causes Antigravity to perform deep reasoning, run bash commands, or inspect multiple files.
- Each tool execution takes several seconds. After 45 iterations (45 seconds), the loop blindly aborts with an error even when the agent is actively working and healthy.

### Issue B: Antigravity replies appear as a single monolithic markdown text bubble
In `AntigravityApiService.kt`:
- The parser only looks for `CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_PLANNER_RESPONSE` and completely ignores `CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_TOOL_CALL` and `CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_TOOL_RESULT`.
In `JarvisViewModel.kt`:
- Thinking is prepended as raw text: `"> **💭 DeepMind Reasoning**\n> " + event.fullThought + "\n\n" + event.fullText`.
- There are no separate tool execution chips or thinking accordions in `TextChatScreen.kt`.

